\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) is the standard 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markup_language
\f2 \'94> 
\f1 markup language
\f2  </a>
\f1  [a] for documents designed to be displayed in a 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser
\f2 \'94> web browser</a>
\f1 . It defines the content and structure of 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_content
\f2 \'94> web content.</a>
\f1 . It is often assisted by technologies such as 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS
\f2 \'94> Cascading Style Sheets (CSS)</a>
\f1  and 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scripting_language
\f2 \'94>scripting language </a>
\f1  such as 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JavaScript
\f2 \'94> JavaScript. </a> \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl399\sa213\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser
\f2 \'94> Web browsers </a> 
\f1  receive HTML documents from a 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_server
\f2 \'94> web server </a>
\f1  or from local storage and 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine
\f2 \'94> render </a> 
\f1 the documents into 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multimedia
\f2 \'94> multimedia </a> 
\f1 web pages. HTML describes the structure of a 
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_page
\f2 \'94> web pages </a> 
\f1  
\f2 <a href=\'93
\f1 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_Web
\f2 \'94> semantically </a>
\f1  and originally included cues for its appearance.
